{"slug":"/students/subjects/chemistry/foundations/laws-of-combination/","source":"students/subjects/chemistry/foundations/laws-of-combination.html","area":"students","kind":"topic","title":"Laws of Chemical Combination | Chemistry Foundations","description":"","subject":"chemistry","body":"<div class=\"max-w-4xl mx-auto\">\n    <!-- Navigation -->\n    <nav class=\"mb-4 flex items-center justify-between\">\n      <a href=\"/students/subjects/chemistry/foundations/\" class=\"text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 transition flex items-center\">\n        <span class=\"mi -arrow-left mr-2\" data-mi=\"arrow_back\">arrow_back</span>Back to Foundations\n      </a>\n      <div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\">\n        <div class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">\n          <span id=\"topic-progress-text\" data-bidemy=\"progress-text\">0% Complete</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"w-24 h-2 bg-gray-200 rounded-full overflow-hidden\" data-bidemy=\"progress\">\n          <div id=\"topic-progress-bar\" class=\"h-full bg-gradient-to-r from-amber-400 to-orange-500 transition-all duration-300\" style=\"width: 0%\"></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </nav>\n    \n    <article class=\"content-card rounded-xl p-6 md:p-8 shadow-lg\">\n      <!-- Header -->\n      <div class=\"border-b pb-4 mb-6\">\n        <h1 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-2\">\n          <span class=\"mi -balance-scale text-amber-500 mr-3\" data-mi=\"balance\">balance</span>Laws of Chemical Combination\n        </h1>\n        <p class=\"text-gray-600\">The fundamental laws governing how elements combine to form compounds.</p>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Learning Objectives -->\n      <div class=\"bg-amber-50 border-l-4 border-amber-500 p-4 rounded-r-lg mb-6\">\n        <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-amber-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -bullseye mr-2\" data-mi=\"adjust\">adjust</span>Learning Objectives</h3>\n        <ul class=\"text-amber-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n          <li>• State and explain the Law of Conservation of Mass</li>\n          <li>• State and explain the Law of Constant Composition</li>\n          <li>• State the Law of Multiple Proportions</li>\n          <li>• Apply these laws to solve problems</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Section 1: Introduction -->\n      <section id=\"section-1\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-amber-100 text-amber-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">1</span>\n          Introduction\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg\">\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">When elements react to form compounds, they follow certain fundamental laws. These <strong class=\"text-amber-600\">Laws of Chemical Combination</strong> form the basis of quantitative chemistry and were discovered through careful experiments by early chemists.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">These laws helped establish <strong>Dalton's Atomic Theory</strong> and our modern understanding of atoms and molecules.</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 2: Law of Conservation of Mass -->\n      <section id=\"section-2\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-amber-100 text-amber-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">2</span>\n          Law of Conservation of Mass\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-green-100 to-teal-100 p-4 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n            <p class=\"text-lg text-center font-semibold text-green-800\">\n              \"Mass is neither created nor destroyed in a chemical reaction.\"\n            </p>\n            <p class=\"text-center text-green-700 text-sm mt-1\">— Antoine Lavoisier (1774)</p>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-4\">\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border\">\n              <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">Statement</h4>\n              <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">In any chemical reaction, the total mass of the reactants equals the total mass of the products.</p>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border\">\n              <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">Implication</h4>\n              <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">Atoms are neither created nor destroyed; they simply rearrange to form new substances.</p>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Worked Example -->\n        <div class=\"border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden\">\n          <button class=\"accordion-btn w-full p-4 bg-green-50 text-left font-semibold text-green-800 flex justify-between items-center hover:bg-green-100 transition\">\n            <span><span class=\"mi -calculator mr-2 text-green-500\" data-mi=\"calculate\">calculate</span>Worked Example</span>\n            <span class=\"mi -chevron-down transform transition-transform\" data-mi=\"expand_more\">expand_more</span>\n          </button>\n          <div class=\"accordion-content\">\n            <div class=\"p-5\">\n              <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">When 4 g of hydrogen reacts with 32 g of oxygen, what mass of water is formed?</p>\n              \n              <div class=\"space-y-3\">\n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-green-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Apply the law:</strong> Mass of reactants = Mass of products</p>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-blue-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Calculate:</strong></p>\n                  <p class=\"text-blue-700 mt-1\">Mass of H₂O = Mass of H₂ + Mass of O₂</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-blue-700\">Mass of H₂O = 4 g + 32 g = <strong>36 g</strong></p>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 3: Law of Constant Composition -->\n      <section id=\"section-3\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-amber-100 text-amber-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">3</span>\n          Law of Constant Composition\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-100 to-indigo-100 p-4 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n            <p class=\"text-lg text-center font-semibold text-blue-800\">\n              \"A given compound always contains the same elements in the same proportion by mass.\"\n            </p>\n            <p class=\"text-center text-blue-700 text-sm mt-1\">— Joseph Proust (1799)</p>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 mb-4\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">Also Known As:</h4>\n            <ul class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n              <li>• Law of Definite Proportions</li>\n              <li>• Law of Constant Composition</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 border-l-4 border-yellow-400 p-4 rounded-r-lg\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-yellow-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -lightbulb mr-2\" data-mi=\"lightbulb\">lightbulb</span>Example</h4>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">Water (H₂O) always contains hydrogen and oxygen in the ratio <strong>1:8 by mass</strong> (or 11.1% H and 88.9% O by mass), whether it comes from a river, a glacier, or a laboratory.</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Worked Example -->\n        <div class=\"border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden\">\n          <button class=\"accordion-btn w-full p-4 bg-blue-50 text-left font-semibold text-blue-800 flex justify-between items-center hover:bg-blue-100 transition\">\n            <span><span class=\"mi -calculator mr-2 text-blue-500\" data-mi=\"calculate\">calculate</span>Worked Example</span>\n            <span class=\"mi -chevron-down transform transition-transform\" data-mi=\"expand_more\">expand_more</span>\n          </button>\n          <div class=\"accordion-content\">\n            <div class=\"p-5\">\n              <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">If 9 g of water is decomposed, what masses of hydrogen and oxygen are obtained?</p>\n              \n              <div class=\"space-y-3\">\n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-blue-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Known ratio:</strong> H₂O contains H:O = 1:8 by mass</p>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-indigo-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Calculate:</strong></p>\n                  <p class=\"text-indigo-700 mt-1\">Total parts = 1 + 8 = 9 parts</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-indigo-700\">Mass of H = (1/9) × 9 g = <strong>1 g</strong></p>\n                  <p class=\"text-indigo-700\">Mass of O = (8/9) × 9 g = <strong>8 g</strong></p>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 4: Law of Multiple Proportions -->\n      <section id=\"section-4\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-amber-100 text-amber-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">4</span>\n          Law of Multiple Proportions\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-purple-100 to-pink-100 p-4 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n            <p class=\"text-lg text-center font-semibold text-purple-800\">\n              \"When two elements combine to form more than one compound, the masses of one element that combine with a fixed mass of the other are in simple whole number ratios.\"\n            </p>\n            <p class=\"text-center text-purple-700 text-sm mt-1\">— John Dalton (1803)</p>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">Example: Carbon and Oxygen</h4>\n            <table class=\"w-full text-sm\">\n              <thead class=\"bg-purple-100\">\n                <tr>\n                  <th class=\"p-2 text-left\">Compound</th>\n                  <th class=\"p-2 text-center\">Carbon (g)</th>\n                  <th class=\"p-2 text-center\">Oxygen (g)</th>\n                </tr>\n              </thead>\n              <tbody>\n                <tr><td class=\"p-2 border\">CO (carbon monoxide)</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">12</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">16</td></tr>\n                <tr><td class=\"p-2 border\">CO₂ (carbon dioxide)</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">12</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">32</td></tr>\n              </tbody>\n            </table>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm mt-3\">The ratio of oxygen in CO and CO₂ = 16:32 = <strong>1:2</strong> (simple whole numbers!)</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Worked Example -->\n        <div class=\"border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden\">\n          <button class=\"accordion-btn w-full p-4 bg-purple-50 text-left font-semibold text-purple-800 flex justify-between items-center hover:bg-purple-100 transition\">\n            <span><span class=\"mi -calculator mr-2 text-purple-500\" data-mi=\"calculate\">calculate</span>Worked Example</span>\n            <span class=\"mi -chevron-down transform transition-transform\" data-mi=\"expand_more\">expand_more</span>\n          </button>\n          <div class=\"accordion-content\">\n            <div class=\"p-5\">\n              <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Nitrogen forms two oxides. In NO, 14 g N combines with 16 g O. In NO₂, 14 g N combines with 32 g O. Show this illustrates the Law of Multiple Proportions.</p>\n              \n              <div class=\"space-y-3\">\n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-purple-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Fixed mass of N:</strong> 14 g in both compounds</p>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-indigo-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Masses of O:</strong> 16 g in NO, 32 g in NO₂</p>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-blue-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Ratio:</strong> 16:32 = <strong>1:2</strong></p>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-green-100 p-3 rounded-lg\">\n                  <p class=\"text-green-800 font-semibold\">Simple whole number ratio = Law of Multiple Proportions verified!</p>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 5: Summary Table -->\n      <section id=\"section-5\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-amber-100 text-amber-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">5</span>\n          Summary of Laws\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"overflow-x-auto\">\n          <table class=\"w-full text-sm border-collapse border border-gray-300 rounded-lg overflow-hidden\">\n            <thead class=\"bg-amber-600 text-white\">\n              <tr>\n                <th class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3 text-left\">Law</th>\n                <th class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3 text-left\">Scientist</th>\n                <th class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3 text-left\">Statement</th>\n              </tr>\n            </thead>\n            <tbody class=\"bg-white\">\n              <tr>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3 font-medium\">Conservation of Mass</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3\">Lavoisier</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3\">Mass is neither created nor destroyed</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr class=\"bg-gray-50\">\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3 font-medium\">Constant Composition</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3\">Proust</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3\">Compounds have fixed composition by mass</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3 font-medium\">Multiple Proportions</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3\">Dalton</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3\">Masses combine in simple whole number ratios</td>\n              </tr>\n            </tbody>\n          </table>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 6: Practice Problems -->\n      <section id=\"section-6\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"mi -pencil-alt text-amber-600 mr-3\" data-mi=\"edit\">edit</span>\n          Practice Problems\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">1. 10 g of CaCO₃ on heating gives 5.6 g of CaO and 4.4 g of CO₂. Show this illustrates the Law of Conservation of Mass.</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>Mass of reactant = 10 g</p>\n                <p>Mass of products = 5.6 + 4.4 = 10 g</p>\n                <p>Mass of reactant = Mass of products ✓</p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">2. CuO always contains 79.9% Cu and 20.1% O by mass. Which law does this illustrate?</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p><strong>Law of Constant Composition</strong> - the compound CuO always has the same composition by mass.</p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">3. In CO, 12 g C combines with 16 g O. In CO₂, 12 g C combines with 32 g O. What is the ratio of oxygen masses?</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>Ratio = 16:32 = <strong>1:2</strong></p>\n                <p>(Simple whole number ratio - Law of Multiple Proportions)</p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Key Takeaways -->\n      <section id=\"section-7\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-amber-50 to-orange-50 p-5 rounded-lg border border-amber-200\">\n          <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-amber-800 mb-3\"><span class=\"mi -star mr-2\" data-mi=\"star\">star</span>Key Takeaways for WAEC/JAMB/NECO</h3>\n          <ul class=\"text-amber-700 text-sm space-y-2\">\n            <li>• <strong>Conservation of Mass:</strong> Mass reactants = Mass products</li>\n            <li>• <strong>Constant Composition:</strong> Same compound = same % composition always</li>\n            <li>• <strong>Multiple Proportions:</strong> Different compounds of same elements = simple mass ratios</li>\n            <li>• Know the scientists associated with each law</li>\n            <li>• Be able to calculate and verify these laws</li>\n          </ul>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Complete Topic Button -->\n      <div class=\"mt-8 pt-6 border-t border-gray-200\">\n        <div class=\"flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4\">\n          <div class=\"text-center sm:text-left\">\n            <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800\">Ready to Complete?</h3>\n            <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">View all sections, then take the quiz to mark this topic as complete.</p>\n          </div>\n          <button id=\"topic-complete-btn\" disabled=\"\" class=\"px-6 py-3 rounded-xl bg-gray-300 text-gray-500 cursor-not-allowed opacity-50 flex items-center gap-2 text-lg font-medium\">\n            <span class=\"mi -lock mr-2\" data-mi=\"lock\">lock</span>\n            <span>Complete (0% viewed)</span>\n          </button>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </article>\n  </div>\n\n  \n\n  \n\n\n<div data-bidemy=\"quiz\"></div>","bodyClass":"min-h-screen bg-gradient-to-br from-amber-50 to-orange-100 p-4 md:p-6","bodyStyle":"","css":["body { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; }\n    .content-card {\n      -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(12px);\n      backdrop-filter: blur(12px);\n      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95);\n      border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);\n    }\n    .accordion-content {\n      max-height: 0;\n      overflow: hidden;\n      transition: max-height 0.3s ease-out;\n    }\n    .accordion-content.open {\n      max-height: 2000px;\n    }\n    .step-card { transition: all 0.2s ease; }\n    .step-card:hover { transform: translateX(4px); }\n    #topic-complete-btn { transition: all 0.3s ease; }\n    #topic-complete-btn:not(:disabled):hover { transform: scale(1.02); }"],"quiz":{"topicId":"laws-of-combination","subject":"chemistry","passingScore":60,"questions":[{"question":"Who proposed the Law of Conservation of Mass?","options":["Dalton","Proust","Lavoisier","Boyle"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Antoine Lavoisier proposed the Law of Conservation of Mass in 1774."},{"question":"In a chemical reaction, 20 g of reactants produce:","options":["Less than 20 g products","More than 20 g products","Exactly 20 g products","Variable mass of products"],"correct":2,"explanation":"By the Law of Conservation of Mass, mass of reactants = mass of products."},{"question":"The Law of Constant Composition is also called:","options":["Law of Multiple Proportions","Law of Definite Proportions","Law of Conservation","Law of Reciprocal Proportions"],"correct":1,"explanation":"The Law of Constant Composition is also known as the Law of Definite Proportions."},{"question":"Water always contains H and O in ratio 1:8 by mass. This illustrates which law?","options":["Conservation of Mass","Multiple Proportions","Constant Composition","Boyle's Law"],"correct":2,"explanation":"The fixed composition of water illustrates the Law of Constant Composition."},{"question":"CO contains 12g C + 16g O. CO₂ contains 12g C + 32g O. What law does this illustrate?","options":["Conservation of Mass","Constant Composition","Multiple Proportions","Gay-Lussac's Law"],"correct":2,"explanation":"The ratio 16:32 = 1:2 shows the Law of Multiple Proportions."},{"question":"If 18 g of water decomposes, what mass of hydrogen is obtained?","options":["1 g","2 g","16 g","9 g"],"correct":1,"explanation":"H₂O has H:O = 1:8 by mass. Total = 9 parts. H = (1/9) × 18 = 2 g"},{"question":"Who proposed the Law of Multiple Proportions?","options":["Lavoisier","Proust","Dalton","Gay-Lussac"],"correct":2,"explanation":"John Dalton proposed the Law of Multiple Proportions in 1803."},{"question":"The Law of Conservation of Mass implies that:","options":["Atoms are destroyed in reactions","Atoms are created in reactions","Atoms are rearranged but not created or destroyed","Mass can change during reactions"],"correct":2,"explanation":"The law means atoms simply rearrange to form new substances - they are neither created nor destroyed."}]},"tracker":{"topicId":"laws-of-combination","topicTitle":"Laws of Chemical Combination","subject":"chemistry","sections":["section-1","section-2","section-3","section-4","section-5","section-6","section-7"],"quizRequired":true},"links":[]}